    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain the difference between high glycemic index and low glycemic index foods? specifically why it matters for insulin.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High glycemic index (GI) foods cause a rapid spike in blood sugar because they are quickly broken down into glucose. In contrast, low GI foods are digested slowly, leading to a gradual rise in blood sugar. This is important for insulin because rapid spikes force the pancreas to release large amounts of insulin quickly. Consuming low GI foods promotes more stable blood sugar levels, reducing the constant stress on the insulin system.",
      "source": "target",
